# Citation metadata for Depictio. GitHub reads it for the "Cite this repository"
# button, and Zenodo reads it when it archives a release.
# `version` is kept in sync by bump2version (.bumpversion.cfg).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Depictio in your research, please cite it using the metadata below, with the version you used."
type: software
title: "Depictio"
abstract: >-
  Depictio is an open-source, self-hosted platform that turns the outputs of
  bioinformatics workflows into interactive, shareable dashboards, built with
  or without writing code.
authors:
  - family-names: Weber
    given-names: Thomas
    affiliation: European Molecular Biology Laboratory (EMBL)
repository-code: "https://github.com/depictio/depictio"
url: "https://depictio.github.io/depictio-docs/latest/"
license: MIT
version: 1.24.0
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - data visualization
  - dashboards
  - workflows
  - nf-core
  - FAIR
